><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250523103500+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250523103509+10'00'" name="3a085c37-1e41-47e9-9de2-a2f1b7536d30" page="7" coords="313.001495,128.231888,575.983154,128.231888,313.001495,117.201965,575.983154,117.201965,313.001495,117.176773,575.942383,117.176773,313.001495,106.146851,575.942383,106.146851,313.001526,106.178665,575.999146,106.178665,313.001526,95.148743,575.999146,95.148743,313.001526,95.123550,576.009216,95.123550,313.001526,84.093628,576.009216,84.093628,313.001526,84.068436,575.968323,84.068436,313.001526,73.038513,575.968323,73.038513,313.001526,73.013321,575.964355,73.013321,313.001526,61.983398,575.964355,61.983398,313.001526,61.958206,575.956116,61.958206,313.001526,50.928284,575.956116,50.928284,313.001526,50.903107,575.968628,50.903107,313.001526,39.873184,575.968628,39.873184" rect="312.656799,39.528488,576.353882,128.576584" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>In conclusion, the results of this study suggest that RMR and&#xD;body composition estimates do not significantly differ between&#xD;Phase 1 and Phase 4 of the MC or with HC use in female athletes.&#xD;Accordingly, measurements of RMR and body composition via&#xD;DXA can be compared in Phase 1 or Phase 4 of the MC, or varying&#xD;HC approaches in female athletes, without variations in sex&#xD;hormones or shifts in fluid balance causing additional noise.&#xD;Furthermore, female athletes do not need to purposefully alter </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>energy intake during Phase 1 or Phase 4 of the MC or with HC&#xD;usage to address changes in RMR and should continue to focus on&#xD;matching energy intake with nutritional goals and training/competition&#xD;need. Finally, as subtle menstrual irregularities are difficult to&#xD;identify, tracking of MC phase for clinical or research activities&#xD;should not assume that an athlete is within a particular phase of the&#xD;MC unless confirmed using Best Practice Guidelines (</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Elliott-Sale&#xD;et al., 2021</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>).</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="7" rect="612.000000,36.231888,796.000000,128.231888"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250523103330+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250523103344+10'00'" name="2d95b762-8096-498a-ad22-e347aa37ae44" page="8" coords="82.150558,694.878418,298.990753,694.878418,82.150558,683.848450,298.990753,683.848450,36.000000,683.880249,298.923035,683.880249,36.000000,672.850342,298.923035,672.850342,36.000000,672.882202,299.005798,672.882202,36.000000,661.852234,299.005798,661.852234,36.000000,661.884033,298.988953,661.884033,36.000000,650.854126,298.988953,650.854126,35.998993,650.885986,87.527573,650.885986,35.998993,639.856018,87.527573,639.856018" rect="35.654297,639.511353,299.350494,695.223145" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
